Error [E3220]: No inline foreign binder for `brainfuck` yet
  --> tests/ui/ffi_unknown_language.jet:1:23
    |
  1 | #[Unsafe("demo"), FFI(brainfuck)] fn f() Int -> {
    |                       ^^^^^^^^^
 Why: The inline foreign tier ships `c`, `cpp`, and `asm` first (the systems floor, card #501); other languages arrive on later polyglot cards
 Fix: Use `#FFI(c)`, `#FFI(cpp)`, or `#FFI(asm)`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E3220
